# Shared UI and DRY

- Do not duplicate the same UI color, magic value, configuration object, or
  non-trivial JSX pattern across screens.
- Keep colors as semantic design tokens in `apps/mobile/global.css`; never create
  screen-local color constants or repeat raw RGB, hex, or palette-based values.
- Put reusable gluestack primitives and variants in
  `apps/mobile/components/ui/`.
- Put reusable product-level compositions in `apps/mobile/src/components/`.
- Put shared non-visual values and typed configuration in
  `apps/mobile/src/constants/`, grouped by domain rather than in one catch-all
  file.
- Keep feature-specific values colocated until a second real usage appears.
  Extract on demonstrated reuse; do not create speculative abstractions.
- Prefer a shared component with explicit typed props over copied JSX with
  slightly different class names.
- Extend an existing semantic token or component when its meaning matches.
  Create a new abstraction only when the role or behavior is genuinely distinct.
- When touching duplicated code, consolidate it within the task scope unless
  doing so would require an unrelated refactor.
